description: On xsofy's world dump the llvm driver spends 46.45 s in assemble (`llvm-module` and its shake), against 6.97 s for gc: 71% of a 65.8 s compile (git-issue:7be2318). For a large program it is the largest llvm cost.
 
 Assemble keeps the live units of the cached runtime and the program and joins their text. On 2026-10-09 it kept 398 of 3,049 runtime fn units for `(println 1)`. The world dump keeps far more, and `LW_PHASE_TIMES` does not yet say which part of assemble takes the time.
 
 Measurements that close it, each with its conditions (revision, load average, run count, through checks/quiet.sh):
 
 - M1 assemble split into its parts (the liveness walk, the unit and global selection, the text join), on the world dump, median of 5.
 - M2 after a change: assemble on the world dump, median of 5, with the shake's output unchanged (the oracle rows for the llvm lane MATCH, P12.38 among them).
